# The plan of a parenthesized join whose LATERAL item reaches the relation to its left (spec/design/
# grammar.md §15): the group is one correlated lateral Subquery relation, a join-search fence planned
# like a top-level LATERAL item, whose body is re-run once per left row — its estimates and actual
# cost scale with the left side. A RIGHT JOIN's lateral item correlated only to the relations outside
# that join is an ordinary Subquery inside the group, evaluated once per evaluation of the group; a
# later comma item holding a RIGHT JOIN is such a group. jed-specific (EXPLAIN estimates and cost), so
# CROSS-CORE-checked, NOT oracle-checked.
# requires: ddl.create_table, ddl.primary_key, dml.insert, dml.insert_multi_row, query.select, query.join_inner, query.join_left, query.join_right, query.comma_from, query.qualified_column, query.derived_table, query.lateral, query.join_parenthesized, query.select_no_from, query.explain, resource.cost_metering, types.i32

